# Every text file is LF in the repository and in every checkout, whatever the
# contributor's core.autocrlf says. DVC hashes files byte for byte, so a Windows
# checkout with CRLF endings makes every Python dependency in dvc.lock look
# changed, and `dvc repro` would rebuild the whole pipeline.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Pipeline outputs committed to Git (`cache: false` in dvc.yaml) are recorded in
# dvc.lock by their exact bytes, so Git must not touch their line endings.
# The CSVs of `evaluate` and `compare-energy` are written by the csv module, which
# ends rows with CRLF everywhere; CodeCarbon writes `reports/emissions/` through
# pandas, which ends them with the platform's separator, so CRLF on Windows.
# Every output with `cache: false` in dvc.yaml belongs here, and
# tests/test_committed_outputs.py fails for one that is missing.
metrics.json -text
reports/metrics/** -text
reports/data-validation/** -text
reports/emissions/** -text
reports/figures/** -text

# The report's figures are PDFs, and the ones a stage draws are byte-for-byte
# copies of its output above (tests/test_committed_outputs.py compares them), so
# Git must not guess one to be text and normalise its line endings.
reports/latex/figures/*.pdf -text
